ng the  time that they won their championships I  totally disagree with that I just  thought that that other crew in my  me you know maybe not quite as talented  if you factor in Kyrie who I think it's  a supremely talented guard but just  their their approach their mental  toughness their willingness to sacrifice  and understand the roles of each the  other players on that Miami team to me  doesn't compare to this Cleveland team  now perhaps the Cleveland team the  Cavaliers this edition will grow to  understand that and develop that but  it's obvious to me that they haven't  quite yet and question themselves  talking with Stu Jackson TV analyst for  NBA TV prior to that obviously a team  executive head coach but also the VP of  basketball operations the role that Kiki  Vandeweghe has the discipline guy  basically which by the way I was blown  away we're gonna net momentarily but  reading Kiki's report about private  investigators everything that goes into  it I'm like floored by that let's start  stew with the with the draymond play  because i guess i saw on twitter where  you said you thought he should have been  suspended yeah i did you know i thought  he should be suspended for a variety of  reasons one is I was really intrigued by  the release at the NBA you know put out  where it mentioned that dream on flailed  well that's sort of a half-truth he  flailed with his arms but when he was  stationary on the floor he then kicked  after the flail with his arms and that  kick you know delivered a blow to the  groin that I thought was really severe I  was severe enough to drop atoms to his  knees it was clearly the wind up with  the leg to follow through a high  potential for injury when you kick  somebody in that area that hard and you  know I just thought Adams was in a  vulnerable position and couldn't defend  himself so you know for that reason when  you add up those factors that meet the  criteria for a flagrant foul and you  look at how hard he was kicked III 